# webmotors-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below. smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: you need ONE of the two network settings below, unless
# you run this from a residential connection of your own.
#
# webmotors.com.br sits behind CloudFront, which refused every datacentre
# address measured on 2026-09-28 (a VPS, headful Chromium included), and
# PerimeterX, which refuses a browser that announces itself as headless.
# The engines handle the second. The first is an address problem, and only
# a residential exit or the Scraping Browser changes it. Exits in Brazil and
# in the United States were both served, so the country does not matter.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# On this site the key is used by --fingerprint only. The one challenge the
# site showed is PerimeterX's Press & Hold, which this repo does not
# implement, and no client this repo drives was shown it once served.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint. Measured 2026-09-28 through
# a country-us profile: served.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. Any country measured was served.
#   pid-      a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account. Reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one.
#
# Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes a bare
# host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer can.
#
# The credentials in a profile expire in about a day, so never paste a
# working one anywhere that is committed.
WEBMOTORS_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-br-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A RESIDENTIAL exit. One URL here, or --proxy-file with one per line for a
# pool. A pool is what spreads a run's volume, and --concurrency without one
# just sends N times the request rate from a single address.
#
# The credentials never reach the browser's command line: they go through
# the driver's own fields, and logs mask them while keeping host and port.
# Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that engine
# strips the credentials and warns — use Playwright or pyppeteer here.
# The country goes in the login (`-region-br`), as measured on 2026-09-28
# through na.proxy.2captcha.com; eu.proxy.2captcha.com answered the same.
WEBMOTORS_PROXY=http://{user}-zone-custom-region-br:{password}@na.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url: any search page or advert on the site, e.g.
#
#   https://www.webmotors.com.br/carros/estoque/volkswagen/gol
#   https://www.webmotors.com.br/carros/sp/toyota?anode=2020
#   https://www.webmotors.com.br/motos/estoque/honda
#
# While it is set, the search flags (--make, --model, --state ...) are
# refused, since they would have to agree with it and nothing checks that
# they do. Leave it unset if you use the flags.
WEBMOTORS_URL=https://www.webmotors.com.br/carros/estoque/volkswagen/gol

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader, which only fills UNSET values, would
# never see it. The variable would be silently inert.
